# Decide Effect Schema Core

Lock the v1 Effect Schema model for the content-grill context plane: shared base types, per-source receipt unions, slurp lifecycle records, privacy tiers, and CLI JSON envelopes. Output is a schema design asset agents can implement without reinterpretation.

## Step

Grill Joel on:

- universal `ContextReceipt` shape vs discriminated union per source
- required vs optional fields on every receipt (summary, index_text, occurred_at, refs)
- `PrivacyTier` levels and redaction rules at index time
- `SlurpCursor` / `SlurpRun` / XState event alignment
- reserved `TopicPrompt` shape (grill output, no body copy)
- CLI envelope pattern (`ok`, `command`, `result`, `next_actions`) compatibility with jc-slack

Resolved when schema modules and field glossary are written to an asset file and Joel confirms v1 can implement without another schema pass.

## Result (2026-08-19)

**Locked:** hexagonal ports/adapters; `ContextReceipt` as Effect `Schema.TaggedUnion` (`Brain`, `XPost`, `AgentSession`, + v2 variants); three privacy tiers with adapter-time redaction; `TopicPromptBatch.generatesCopy: false`; XState slurp machine aligned to `SlurpCursor.status`.

**Prototype:** `joelhooks/content-grill` — `src/domain/*`, `src/ports/index.ts`, `src/machines/slurp-run.ts`; 5 schema tests green; CLI `doctor` stub.

**Asset:** [Effect Schema v1 Design](./effect-schema-v1-design.svx)

**Deferred:** string maxLength filters (Effect v4 filter API pass); full CLI envelopes wired to store.
